  "reason": "Evidence: The current best RNA-only model uses scvi_n200 (config_005: 0.650 acc, config_006: 0.653 acc), and multiprofile+avgpool is the strongest combination. However, we have no data on the scgpt encoder, leaving a key representation question unresolved. Question: config_008 (scgpt, multiprofile, avgpool) is a direct single-variable comparison to config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool), isolating the effect of the RNA encoder while holding profile setting and aggregation constant. Why this is the best next experiment: It directly tests whether a different RNA representation can beat our current best (0.650), which would reshape all subsequent multimodal and encoder choices. If scgpt underperforms, we confirm scvi_n200 as the preferred encoder and can confidently proceed to test whether adding image signal (even with a stronger ViT-L encoder) provides any marginal gain over the 0.653 RNA-only ceiling. This is more informative than jumping to multimodal configs (which add two new variables at once) or testing image-only ViT-L (which, given resnet50's 0.208, may not change the strategic picture as directly as knowing our best RNA encoder)."
}

